# ==================================================================================================
# Stopping power fits on specific incident/target ion pairs
# This file contains data for the Konac form of the stopping power description
# for all ions.  The entries in this field will be used before resorting to 
# the default Ziegler stopping power calculations (scaled proton data).  To
# ==================================================================================================
# Stopping power fit coefficients
#
# Primary Reference:
#   Konac 98:  G. Konac, S. Kalbitzer, Ch. Klatt, D. Niemann, R. Stoll,
#              NIM B, 136-138 (1998) 159-165.
#
# Secondary data references:
#   Konac 98a: Konac 98, assuming velocity scaling from 1H and 4He
#
#===================================================================================================
#  Inc Target                       Coefficients as per Konac 98 reference         (a3)
# Z  M   Z    scaling     s       a0        a1        a2        a3        a4        a5      beta
#===================================================================================================
  1  1   6    1.000     0.39    3.40E-2 -3.93E-2   2.09E-2       0         0     7.89E-1    36.5  # Konac 98
  1  2   6    1.000     0.39    3.40E-2 -3.93E-2   2.09E-2       0         0     7.89E-1    36.5  # Konac 98a
  2  4   6    1.000     0.49    1.36E-3  2.47E-2  -1.81E-2       0         0     1.88E-1    36.5  # Konac 98
  2  3   6    1.000     0.49    1.36E-3  2.47E-2  -1.81E-2       0         0     1.88E-1    36.5  # Konac 98a
  1  1  14    1.000     0.37    4.16E-2 -1.47E-1   1.80E-1       0         0     2.79E-1    15.7  # Konac 98
  1  2  14    1.000     0.37    3.66E-2 -1.24E-1   1.52E-1       0         0     2.93E-1    15.7  # Konac 98
  2  3  14    1.000     0.52    8.24E-3 -2.02E-2   2.28E-2       0         0     8.18E-2    15.7  # Konac 98
  2  4  14    1.000     0.52    7.93E-3 -1.93E-2   2.21E-2       0         0     8.25E-2    15.7  # Konac 98
